Done. Three deliverables, all inside `ros2_stack/`.

## What I added

**`launch/nav2.launch.py`** — wires `gps_gate` → `navsat_transform_node` → `ekf_node`, then a Nav2 controller/planner/lifecycle block. The header comment block lists required apt packages (`ros-humble-robot-localization` is the only one not already in `docker/Dockerfile.humble`), the REP-105 frame tree with per-transform ownership, and the two blocking caveats below.

**`README.md`** — added the `Next batch` section summarizing localization + control.

**`docs/localization_control_plan.md`** — merges the localization and control points from `mowglinext_baseline.md` §3/§4.3/§6/§7.2, and records where the stack actually stands.

## Two things I had to decide, and one I could not ask about

`src/mower_localization` did not exist when I started, so `launch/nav2.launch.py` would have referenced a package with no `gps_gate` in it. I created the package (`gps_gate` node, `config/ekf.yaml`, `config/navsat.yaml`, 25 tests passing) so the launch file actually resolves. `mower_control` and `docs/localization.md` appeared from parallel work while I was writing; I read them and built on them rather than duplicating.

I picked **dual-EKF over the baseline's GTSAM factor graph**, reasoning from baseline §7.2's own stated fallback: GTSAM needs an aarch64 source build, and with no 2D LiDAR there is no scan matching to justify it. This is a real divergence from the baseline, documented as such.

## Two blockers worth your attention

**`wit_imu_driver` never populates `Imu.orientation`.** It parses the JY61P 0x53 angle frame and `fill_angle_from_tracked()` only debug-logs it — the quaternion stays zero, covariances are all zero. I verified this against the upstream `humble-devel` source for `navsat_transform_node`: it builds the GPS-to-world heading from exactly that quaternion. So the GPS correction is currently wrong and the EKF fuses a zero absolute yaw while over-trusting the IMU. The fix is in the driver, not the configs.

**No `map → odom` publisher.** `navsat_transform_node` only broadcasts when `broadcast_utm_transform` is true (set false), and `ekf_node` is `world_frame: odom`, so per its documented two-mode behaviour it broadcasts `odom → base_link` only. The stack localizes in `odom` — continuous and GPS-corrected, but anchored wherever the machine was switched on. My earlier draft claimed this was a GPS double-count; checking the source showed that is not what happens, so the doc records the actual gap instead.

One correction worth flagging: `ekf.yaml` takes `/odometry/gps` as `odom1`, not `pose0`, because navsat publishes `nav_msgs/Odometry` while `poseN` inputs are typed `PoseWithCovarianceStamped` — a `pose0` entry would silently never connect.

Nothing was run on the mower, and I verified behaviour against the upstream Humble source rather than memory.

当前会话上下文已达 248K tokens，过长的上下文会增加 AI 理解偏差和致幻概率，影响代码质量和工作效率。

建议：保存当前进展 → 新建会话 → 恢复记忆

第一步：保存记忆
告诉 AI："把当前的工作进展、关键决策、待办事项总结保存到 MEMORY.md"
AI 会自动在项目根目录创建/更新 MEMORY.md 文件。

第二步：新建会话
* Claude Code → 输入 /clear 
* openclaw → 输入 /new
* 其他客户端 →请问ai

第三步：恢复记忆
在新会话的第一句话说："读取 MEMORY.md，继续之前的工作"
AI 会自动加载之前保存的进展，从断点继续。

小技巧：养成每完成一个功能模块就保存记忆的习惯，
不仅能保持响应速度，还能让 AI 的输出质量更稳定。
